## Notebooks

Put Jupyter notebooks in `notebooks/`, then compile them into the docs site
(the script needs at least one `.ipynb` in `notebooks/`):

```bash
uv run scripts/render_notebooks.sh
```
{%- if docs_hosting != 'none' %}

CI only builds what is committed, so commit `docs/compiled_notebooks/` after
rendering.
{%- endif %}

To strip notebook outputs when committing, set up a Git filter:

```bash
# In .git/config
[filter "strip-notebook-output"]
    clean = "jupyter nbconvert --ClearOutputPreprocessor.enabled=True --to=notebook --stdin --stdout --log-level=ERROR"
    smudge = "cat"
    required

# In .git/info/attributes
*.ipynb filter=strip-notebook-output
```

This keeps the repository size small while preserving the notebook code and
structure.
{%- endif %}

## Claude Code
{%- if pauli_braun %}

This project recommends the
[pauli-braun](https://github.com/yamatteo/pauli_braun) Claude Code plugin, a
plan/review (Pauli) and build (Braun) workflow. Claude Code offers to install it
when you trust this folder; run `/pauli` to start.
{%- else %}

The [pauli-braun](https://github.com/yamatteo/pauli_braun) Claude Code plugin
is explicitly disabled in this project by `.claude/settings.json`, even if you
have it installed. To turn it back on for yourself only, set
`"pauli-braun@pauli-braun": true` under `enabledPlugins` in
`.claude/settings.local.json`.
{%- endif %}
{%- if cluster_gateway %}

## Cluster gateway

This project may use the
[cluster-gateway](https://gitlab.fbk.eu/mbortolotto/cluster_gateway) MCP server
to run jobs on remote compute. The gateway is installed and registered once, at
user scope; see its README. To make this project reachable, add an entry to
`~/.config/cluster_gateway_mcp/config.yaml`:

```yaml
projects:
  {{ project_slug }}:
    local_root: <absolute path of this project>
    downloads_subdir: gateway-results
    origin_url: <URL the host clones fetch from>
    allowed_branches: ["main"]
    command: [<argv>, "{target}"]
    env_allowed: []
    artifact_globs: []
    hosts:
      <host>:
        remote_root: <base clone path on the host>
```

Then make the base clone on each host, and run
`cluster-gateway-admin deploy <host>` and `cluster-gateway-admin selftest <host>`.

The gateway's read-only tools are pre-allowed in `.claude/settings.json`;
Claude Code still asks before it submits, cancels or downloads.
{%- endif %}
